tatus="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TEIJIN LIMITED</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YANO, SHINJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, TETSUO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUKUDA MASAYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITAZAWA SATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAIGO TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YANO SHINJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA TETSUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKUDA, MASAYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITAZAWA, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAIGO, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YANO, SHINJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, TETSUO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A white, biaxially orientated polyester film for an image receiving substrate for use in an ink-jet printer, which satisfies the following requirements (1) to (4): (1) the content of titanium oxide particles having an average particle diameter of 0.1 to 0.5  mu m in said polyester film is 5 to 20 wt %, (2) said polyester film has an average gloss of 65 to 95 %, (3) said polyester film has an X-ray diffraction intensity ratio (F-1/F-2) in the range represented by the formula (1): 0.05 &lt;/= F-1/F-2 &lt;/= 0.15 wherein F-1 represents an X-ray diffraction intensity by (110) plane parallel with the surface of the film, and F-2 represents an X-ray diffraction intensity by (100) plane parallel with the face of the film, and (4) said polyester film has a static friction coefficient of 0.3 to 0.6; and an image receiving substrate for use in an ink-jet printer. The image receiving substrate for use in an ink-jet printer is excellent in adhesiveness, gloss, hiding property and conveyability.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Ce film polyester blanc orienté biaxialement pour substrat recevant une image, utilisable avec une imprimante à jet d'encre, satisfait aux exigences suivantes (1 à 4): (1), la teneur de ce film polyester en particules d'oxyde de titane d'un diamètre particulaire moyen compris entre 0,1 et 0.5  mu m est de 5 à 20 % en poids, (2), le lustre moyen de ce film polyester est compris entre 65 et 95 %, (3), le rapport d'intensité de réfraction des rayons X de ce film polyester (F-1/F-2) se trouve dans la plage définie par la formule (1): 0,05 &lt;/= F-1/F-2 &lt;/= 0,15, F-1 représentant une intensité de diffraction des rayons X (110) par plan parallèle à la surface du film et F-2 représentant une intensité de diffraction des rayons X (110) par plan parallèle à la face du film, (4), le coefficient de frottement statique de ce film polyester est compris entre 0,3 et 0,6. L'invention concerne également un substrat recevant une image utilisable avec une imprimante à jet d'encre. Ce substrat a de remarquables qualités d'adhésivité, de lustre, de couvrant et de transportabilité.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its